      "title": "Victorian Greens seek urgent injunction over how-to-vote cards mimicking party’s branding but preferencing it last",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/victorian-greens-seek-urgent-injunction-over-how-to-vote-cards-mimicking-branding-but-preferencing-it-last-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> Independent candidate Tosh-Jake Finnigan’s cards instruct people to vote in a way that would benefit Liberal party</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Victorian Greens are seeking an urgent injunction from the supreme court to stop an independent candidate distributing how-to-vote cards that allegedly mimic the party’s branding and urge people to preference it last.</p><p>As prepoll opened on Wednesday morning, Tosh-Jake Finnigan’s campaign team handed out how-to-vote cards that used the minor party’s colour scheme, font and triangle logo with the banner “Vote 1 Green Values”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/victorian-greens-seek-urgent-injunction-over-how-to-vote-cards-mimicking-branding-but-preferencing-it-last-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-21T00:26:56"
    },
    {
      "title": "NSW passes Mount Pleasant coalmine law as Greens claim change an attempt to head off One Nation",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/nsw-passes-hunter-valley-coalmine-law-as-greens-claim-change-an-attempt-to-head-off-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Labor says allowing mine to increase production reflects ‘gravity of situation facing hundreds of workers’ – but critics call it ‘unprecedented and dangerous’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The New South Wales government has passed special legislation to allow a coalmine in the Hunter Valley to increase production by 32% in its final act of parliament before the March state election, in which the region will be a key battleground for One Nation.</p><p>After a marathon session in the legislative council on Friday, the Minns government and the Coalition voted at 1.36am on Saturday morning to allow the Mount Pleasant mine to increase its annual extraction rate from 12.5MT to 16.5MT until 2032.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/21/nsw-passes-hunter-valley-coalmine-law-as-greens-claim-change-an-attempt-to-head-off-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T23:09:57"
    }
  ]
